    "caption": "What better way to show your love than by preparing a sweet Strawberry Cheesecake Galette for your special someone?\n\nWe’ve whipped up this delicious treat using KitchenAid products, which make the perfect Valentine’s present too, by the way! Tried and tested, KitchenAid’s stylish appliances are known for their durability and reliability in making food preparation a breeze. The best news is that KitchenAid products are now available at #TheMarketplace! Come and get ‘em!\n\nServing Time: 3 hours\nYield: 4-6 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nDOUGH:\n2 cups all-purpose flour \n1 tbsp. granulated sugar \n1 tsp. salt \n3/4 cup unsalted butter, cold and cubed\n1/3 cup cold water\n1/2 tsp. Vinegar\n\nSTRAWBERRY JAM:\n1 cup strawberries, diced\n1/3 cup granulated sugar\n1 tsp. lemon zest\n1 tbsp. lemon juice \n\nCHEESECAKE:\n1/2 bar cream cheese\n1/3 cup powdered sugar, sifted\n1 tsp. lemon zest\n1 tsp. vanilla extract  \n\nASSEMBLY:\n2 tbsps. egg wash\n2 tbsps. brown sugar\n1 cup strawberries, sliced \n2 tbsps. mint leaves \n\nProcedure\n\n1. Add flour, sugar, and salt in the KitchenAid Food Chopper. Pulse to combine. Add in butter, then pulse to slightly break down the butter. Drizzle in cold water and vinegar, then pulse until the mixture starts to come together.\n2. Turn over dough onto a clean surface. Pat it together into a disk. Wrap tightly with cling film, then refrigerate for 1 hour.\n3. Combine strawberries, sugar, lemon zest and lemon juice in a saucepan over medium-high heat. Cook for 12-15 minutes. Once thickened, puree using the KitchenAid Hand Blender. Let cool completely.\n4. Using the KitchenAid Hand Mixer, cream together cream cheese, powdered sugar, lemon zest and vanilla extract. Beat until smooth and creamy.\n5. Place the dough in between 2 large parchment papers. Roll out into a 1/8 inch-thick round. Spread cream cheese on the rolled out dough, leaving an inch border all around. Spread strawberry jam on top of the cream cheese layer. Fold the edges to make a border all around the galette. Freeze for 15 minutes.\n6. Brush the border with egg wash, then sprinkle brown sugar on top of the pastry. Bake at 175C for 30-35 minutes.\n7. Top with sliced strawberries and mint.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
